mdns: keep a device's IPv6 link-local address as a secondary address

A HomePod reports its volume buttons over DACP from its IPv6
link-local address (fe80::...%en0), while the only IPv6 address the
server knew for it was the routable one from the same mDNS
announcement: mdns_dnssd.c ignored link-local addresses outright. So
a request that plainly came from the speaker could not be matched to
it, and player_speaker_get_byaddress() found nothing.

Pass IPv6 link-local addresses through with their scope, file them in
a new output_device.v6_address_ll that nothing ever connects to, and
match against it in speaker_get_byaddress(), comparing addresses
without their scope since the peer address from the HTTP backend
carries one and other sources may not.

--- a/src/mdns_dnssd.c
+++ b/src/mdns_dnssd.c
@@ -537,7 +537,7 @@
 mdns_browse_call_cb(struct mdns_addr_lookup *lu, const char *hostname,
                     const struct sockaddr *address)
 {
-  char addr_str[INET6_ADDRSTRLEN];
+  char addr_str[INET6_ADDRSTRLEN + 1 + IF_NAMESIZE];
 
   if (address->sa_family == AF_INET)
     {
@@ -586,10 +586,19 @@
         }
       else if (is_v6ll(&addr6->sin6_addr))
         {
-          DPRINTF(E_WARN, L_MDNS,
-                  "Ignoring announcement from %s, address %s is link-local\n",
+          // Passed on with its scope, so the outputs layer can tell it from a
+          // routable address: a speaker may talk back to us from it (a HomePod
+          // sends its DACP volume reports from its link-local address), and
+          // we want to recognise it, without ever connecting to it.
+          char ifname[IF_NAMESIZE];
+          size_t len = strlen(addr_str);
+
+          if (lu->rs->interface > 0 && if_indextoname(lu->rs->interface, ifname))
+            snprintf(addr_str + len, sizeof(addr_str) - len, "%%%s", ifname);
+
+          DPRINTF(E_DBG, L_MDNS,
+                  "Announcement from %s, address %s is link-local, keeping it as a secondary address\n",
                   hostname, addr_str);
-          return;
         }
     }
 
